    "kernel_code": "1: \"\"\"Row-wise first-maximum index via a packed integer-key reduction.\n2: \n3: Original synthetic Triton implementation; not an upstream historical bug.\n4: \"\"\"\n5: import torch\n6: import triton\n7: import triton.language as tl\n8: \n9: \n10: @triton.jit\n11: def _argmax_kernel(X, OUT, N: tl.constexpr, BLOCK: tl.constexpr):\n12:     row = tl.program_id(0)\n13:     column = tl.arange(0, BLOCK)\n14:     value = tl.load(X + row * N + column, mask=column < N, other=0.0)\n15:     raw = value.to(tl.uint16, bitcast=True).to(tl.uint32)\n16:     mask = tl.where((raw & 0x8000) != 0, 0xffff, 0x8000).to(tl.uint32)\n17:     rank = raw ^ mask\n18:     # Rank dominates; reversed column indices select the first equal value.\n19:     tie = 0xffffffff - column.to(tl.uint32)\n20:     key = (rank.to(tl.uint64) << 32) | tie.to(tl.uint64)\n21:     key = tl.where(column < N, key, 0)\n22:     best = tl.max(key, axis=0)\n23:     winner = (0xffffffff - (best & 0xffffffff)).to(tl.int64)\n24:     tl.store(OUT + row, winner)\n25: \n26: \n27: def validate_inputs(x, require_cuda=True):\n28:     def require(condition, message):\n29:         if not condition:\n30:             raise ValueError(message)\n31:     require(not torch.is_inference_mode_enabled(), \"ordinary execution mode required\")\n32:     require(type(x) is torch.Tensor, \"ordinary torch.Tensor required\")\n33:     require(x.layout == torch.strided and x.is_contiguous(), \"contiguous strided input required\")\n34:     require(not x.requires_grad and not x.is_inference(), \"ordinary non-gradient input required\")\n35:     require(not x.is_neg() and not x.is_conj(), \"logical view flags outside domain\")\n36:     require(not require_cuda or x.is_cuda, \"CUDA input required\")\n37:     require(x.ndim == 2, \"matrix [M,N] required\")\n38:     require(1 <= x.shape[0] <= 65536 and 1 <= x.shape[1] <= 4096\n39:             and x.numel() <= 262144, \"matrix dimensions outside domain\")\n40:     require(x.dtype == torch.float16, \"FP16 input required\")\n41:     require(bool(torch.isfinite(x).all().item()), \"all values must be finite\")\n42:     return {\"valid\": True, \"shape\": list(x.shape)}\n43: \n44: \n45: def run(x):\n46:     validate_inputs(x)\n47:     m, n = x.shape\n48:     with torch.cuda.device(x.device):\n49:         output = torch.empty((m,), dtype=torch.int64, device=x.device)\n50:         _argmax_kernel[(m,)](x, output, N=n, BLOCK=triton.next_power_of_2(n), num_warps=4)\n51:     return output\n52: \n53: \n54: def reference(x):\n55:     \"\"\"FP16-to-FP64 conversion is exact; numerical ties use the first index.\"\"\"\n56:     validate_inputs(x, require_cuda=False)\n57:     return torch.argmax(x.to(torch.float64), dim=1)\n58: \n59: \n60: def make_inputs(device=\"cuda\", rows=17, columns=257, seed=0):\n61:     \"\"\"Convenience examples, not a restriction on the input domain.\"\"\"\n62:     generator = torch.Generator(device=\"cpu\").manual_seed(seed)\n63:     x = torch.randn((rows, columns), generator=generator).to(torch.float16)\n64:     return (x.to(device),)",
    "passed": "unknown",
    "problem_text": "Compute the first index of the largest value in each row of an FP16 matrix.\nFor every row r, return the smallest column index j for which\n\n  x[r, j] = max(x[r, 0], ..., x[r, N-1]).\n\nThe comparison is ordinary numerical comparison of the exact stored values.\nPositive and negative zero compare equal; if a row's maximum is zero, the\nfirst zero of either sign wins. Every finite FP16 value is legal, including\nboth signed zeros, all positive/negative subnormals, and +/-65504. NaN and\ninfinity are outside the domain. There is no approximate tolerance for the\ninteger index: the returned index must equal the specified first index.\n\nComplete input domain:\n- x is an ordinary torch.Tensor (not a subclass), dense strided contiguous\n  FP16 CUDA tensor with shape [M,N]. Contiguous views with nonzero storage\n  offsets are legal.\n- 1<=M<=65536, 1<=N<=4096, and M*N<=262144.\n- x has requires_grad=False, is_inference=False, is_neg=False, is_conj=False.\n  Calls run in ordinary non-inference mode without concurrent external\n  writes to x. This forward-only operation does not provide autograd.\n\nReturn a fresh torch.int64 CUDA tensor [M] on x.device, and preserve x.\nAny implementation strategy is allowed if it returns the required exact\nindices throughout the complete domain. Correctness is one verdict for the\nimplementation, not a verdict per input, shape, distribution, or seed.\n\nvalidate_inputs() checks this domain and is called by run(). reference()\nuses numerical FP64 comparisons of exactly representable FP16 values and\nalso accepts CPU input. make_inputs() supplies examples only.\n\nThis is an original synthetic Triton implementation of stable argmax using\npacked integer keys. It is not copied from an upstream kernel and is not a\nclaim of a historical upstream bug.\n\nFrozen environment: NVIDIA T4, PyTorch2.8.0, Triton3.4.0.\n",
